    "question": {
      ":question/id": "cbba57a5-7818-5a4d-b0f8-83504b28e5c3",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Complete the square on $x^2-5x+2$.\n\nFill in the nonnegative numbers.\n\n$x^2-5x+2=(x-$ {{field-1}} $)^2-$ {{field-2}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The half of the linear coefficient is $-\\frac{5}{2}$. **Add and subtract** its square so the expression keeps its value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^2-5x+2&=\\underbrace{x^2-2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}x+\\frac{25}{4}}_{\\text{perfect square}}-\\frac{25}{4}+2 \\\\\n&=\\left(x-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{25}{4}+2 \\\\\n&=\\left(x-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{17}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minus sign inside the square produces the required linear term $-5x$.\n\nThe blanks are $\\frac{5}{2}$ and $\\frac{17}{4}$; the sign before the second blank is already supplied.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "59042e24-2305-5dd1-96a0-fd8ea07a175f",
